# How to Preflight an Adobe InDesign Document Before Printing

Last updated: August 2026

Before sending an Adobe InDesign document to print, delivery, packaging, or publication, it is important to check for common production problems.

Missing links, missing fonts, overset text, low-resolution images, incorrect document dimensions, RGB graphics, and missing bleed settings can all cause problems later in the production workflow.

Adobe InDesign provides native Preflight tools that can help identify many of these issues.

The challenge becomes larger when the same checks need to be performed across multiple documents or an entire production project.

This guide explains what to check in an InDesign document before printing and how to approach production preflight for larger projects.

