# InDesign Preflight Checklist

A practical preflight should consider several categories.

## 1. Links

Check whether placed graphics are available.

Look for:

* missing links;
* broken links;
* unavailable source files.

---

## 2. Fonts

Check for:

* missing fonts;
* unavailable fonts;
* substituted fonts.

Font problems can affect text flow and layout.

---

## 3. Overset Text

Check whether text is hidden because it extends beyond the visible text frame.

This is particularly important in layouts where content changes during production.

---

## 4. Image Resolution

Check whether placed graphics meet the effective resolution requirements of the intended output.

The appropriate resolution depends on the production process and output requirements.

---

## 5. Color

Check whether graphics use the expected color configuration.

For example, some print workflows require identifying RGB graphics before production.

---

## 6. Document Dimensions

Verify that the document uses the expected page size.

Incorrect dimensions can create production problems even when the content itself appears correct.

---

## 7. Bleed

Check that the required bleed settings are present.

Bleed requirements depend on the production process and printer specifications.

---

## 8. Pagination

Verify that the document contains the expected number of pages.

For certain production workflows, page-count parity can also matter.

---

## 9. Empty Frames

Check for empty image frames or other objects that may have been left unintentionally in the document.

---

## 10. Hidden Layers

Review hidden layers when they could affect production output or document integrity.

