# What Should a Production Preflight Report Contain?

A useful report should make it easy to identify:

* which document was checked;
* which issue was detected;
* which files require attention;
* which checks were performed.

A report can also provide a record of the verification process.

For production teams, this can make it easier to review, share, and archive preflight results.

