# Frequently Asked Questions

## What should I check before printing an InDesign file?

Common checks include missing links, missing fonts, overset text, image resolution, color information, document dimensions, bleed, and pagination.

The exact requirements depend on the production workflow and printer specifications.

## Does InDesign have a preflight tool?

Yes. Adobe InDesign includes native Preflight functionality for identifying production issues.

## Can I preflight multiple InDesign documents?

Yes. Individual documents can be checked separately, while batch tools can automate repeated checks across larger document collections.

## How do I check an entire InDesign project?

For a small project, check each document individually. For larger projects, a batch workflow can scan project folders and nested subfolders.

## Can preflight detect missing fonts?

Yes. Missing fonts are among the production conditions that can be checked.

## Can preflight detect missing links?

Yes. Missing links can be identified as part of production verification.

## Does preflight replace visual inspection?

No. Technical preflight and visual production review serve different purposes and should be used together.

